Indeed, I've even added tests with unbinding confirming such behavior:
```cpp
		object.connect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback0).unbind(1), Object::CONNECT_APPEND_SOURCE_OBJECT);
		object.emit_signal("my_custom_signal");
		CHECK_EQ(target.received_args, Vector<Variant>{});
		object.disconnect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback0));

		object.connect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback1).unbind(1), Object::CONNECT_APPEND_SOURCE_OBJECT);
		object.emit_signal("my_custom_signal", "emit_arg");
		CHECK_EQ(target.received_args, Vector<Variant>{ "emit_arg" });
		object.disconnect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback1));

		object.connect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback1).bind("bind_arg").unbind(1), Object::CONNECT_APPEND_SOURCE_OBJECT);
		object.emit_signal("my_custom_signal");
		CHECK_EQ(target.received_args, Vector<Variant>{ "bind_arg" });
		object.disconnect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback1));

		object.connect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback2).bind("bind_arg").unbind(1), Object::CONNECT_APPEND_SOURCE_OBJECT);
		object.emit_signal("my_custom_signal", "emit_arg");
		CHECK_EQ(target.received_args, Vector<Variant>{ "emit_arg", "bind_arg" });
		object.disconnect("my_custom_signal", callable_mp(&target, &SignalReceiver::callback2));
```

But you're right, it makes pretty much no sense for it to behave like that. For such behavior you can already use `object.signal.emit(callable.bind(object))`, the `CONNECT_APPEND_SOURCE_OBJECT` flag would be not needed for that.

So it makes sense for the `CONNECT_APPEND_SOURCE_OBJECT` to be appending regardless of the callable's unbinds, on the Object-level (not just hacked-in in the PackedScene etc.).
The docs will need to be clarified though, as you can see it wasn't obvious to me that's the expected behavior (even given it wasn't actually implemented in the Object).

---

Now I'm not sure about the implementation. cc @dalexeev in case you have some thoughts/sugestions regarding that.

- How to "skip the unbinds"? Could be done e.g. by injecting the source-binding past the last chain on unbinds, something like:
```gdscript
callable{.any_bind_unbind_combination()}{.last_bind(arg)}.unbind(last1).unbind(last2)
# to:
callable{.any_bind_unbind_combination()}{.last_bind(arg)}.bind(source).unbind(last1).unbind(last2)
```
Is there a simpler/better way? 🤔

- Performance-wise it makes more sense to append the source once in `connect`, not in `emit_signal` like currently done in this PR. But doing so in `connect` means the source would be somehow already included (e.g. binded) in the connected Callable, which would then require special handling in PackedScene (reverting the source-appending to not store such appended source) or `Node.duplicate` (retarget the source to new duplicated node) etc. Doing so in `emit_signal` means no special handling needed elsewhere as the correct source will be appended as long as the `CONNECT_APPEND_SOURCE_OBJECT` flag was stored/copied.

